From 85e7ce6c689e05bc209feda6d30a3bba51c533c6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 17:50:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] borg: type the birth menu's own letters when respawning

When the Borg respawns it picks its new race and class by typing the
menu letter for each choice.  It used all_letters, but the birth menus
label their entries with all_letters_nohjkl, which skips h, j, k and l.
From the eighth entry on the typed letter was wrong: Half-Troll (h),
High-Elf (j) and Kobold (k) typed a letter the menu does not have, so
the highlighted race was kept, and Dunadan (i) selected Half-Troll; for
classes, Ranger (h) kept the highlighted class and Blackguard (i)
selected Ranger.  The random name was still made for the race wanted.
Use the same letter table as the menus.

Tracked as diegoami/neo-angband-tracker#52.
---
 src/borg/borg-reincarnate.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-reincarnate.c b/src/borg/borg-reincarnate.c
index f474cc5ef..e2b641ed6 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-reincarnate.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-reincarnate.c
@@ -332,13 +332,13 @@ void borg_reincarnate_start(void)
 
     /* pick race */
     if (race != player->race->ridx) {
-        borg_keypress(all_letters[race]);
+        borg_keypress(all_letters_nohjkl[race]);
     }
     borg_keypress(KC_ENTER);
 
     /* pick class */
     if (class != player->class->cidx) {
-        borg_keypress(all_letters[class]);
+        borg_keypress(all_letters_nohjkl[class]);
     }
     borg_keypress(KC_ENTER);
 
